# Practical 6: Integrate External Tools & Artifact Registry

## Objective
Integrate a package manager (pip) and an artifact registry (Docker Hub) into a Jenkins Declarative Pipeline running on Windows.

## Tools & Services Integrated
| Type | Name | Purpose |
|------|------|---------|
| Package Manager | pip (Python) | Install Flask dependencies from requirements.txt |
| Artifact Registry | Docker Hub | Store Docker image (simulated push) |

## Pipeline Stages

1. **Checkout** – Creates `app.py` and `requirements.txt` (simulated Git)
2. **Install Dependencies** – Runs `pip install -r requirements.txt` – real external tool call
3. **Build Docker Image** – Simulated `docker build` command
4. **Tag Image** – Simulated `docker tag` for Docker Hub
5. **Push to Registry** – Simulated `docker push` to Docker Hub

## Pipeline Script (Windows-compatible)

```groovy
pipeline {
    agent any
    environment {
        APP_NAME = 'flask-counter-app'
        VERSION = '1.0'
        DOCKER_HUB_REPO = 'tsheringtenzin/flask-counter-app'
    }
    stages {
        stage('Checkout') {
            steps {
                echo 'Checking out code...'
                bat 'if not exist app mkdir app'
                bat 'echo from flask import Flask > app\\app.py'
                bat 'echo app = Flask(__name__) >> app\\app.py'
                bat 'echo @app.route("/") >> app\\app.py'
                bat 'echo def hello(): return "Hello" >> app\\app.py'
                bat 'echo if __name__ == "__main__": app.run() >> app\\app.py'
                bat 'echo flask==2.3.3 > app\\requirements.txt'
            }
        }
        stage('Install Dependencies') {
            steps {
                echo 'Installing Python packages using pip...'
                bat 'pip install -r app\\requirements.txt'
            }
        }
        stage('Build Docker Image') {
            steps {
                echo 'Building Docker image...'
                bat 'echo docker build -t %APP_NAME%:%VERSION% .'
            }
        }
        stage('Tag Image') {
            steps {
                echo 'Tagging image for Docker Hub...'
                bat 'echo docker tag %APP_NAME%:%VERSION% %DOCKER_HUB_REPO%:%VERSION%'
            }
        }
        stage('Push to Registry') {
            steps {
                echo 'Pushing to Docker Hub...'
                bat 'echo docker push %DOCKER_HUB_REPO%:%VERSION%'
            }
        }
    }
    post {
        success { echo 'Pipeline succeeded!' }
        failure { echo 'Pipeline failed!' }
    }
}
```

## Execution Results
pip install successful – Flask and dependencies installed

All stages executed without errors

Simulated Docker commands output as echo statements

## Configuration Requirements Met
External tool (pip) integrated and executed

Artifact registry (Docker Hub) integrated (simulated push)

Credentials managed (optional, for real push)

Windows-compatible bat commands used

